  "ai_overview": {
    "text_blocks": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Choosing between a metal roof and asphalt shingles in Utah depends on your budget, how long you plan to stay in your home, and how well the material handles heavy snow and ice.",
        "snippet_highlighted_words": [
          "depends on your budget, how long you plan to stay in your home, and how well the material handles heavy snow and ice"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Cost"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Asphalt Shingles: Lower upfront cost. Roof replacement in Utah typically ranges from $8,000 to $40,000+ depending on home size, with asphalt being the most affordable choice."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Metal Roof: Higher initial installation cost, but saves money over time because it rarely needs replacement."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Lifespan & Durability"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Asphalt Shingles: Lasts about 20 to 30 years. They can suffer from granule loss, cracking, and curling due to intense UV rays and freeze-thaw cycles."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Metal Roof: Lasts 40 to 75+ years. Metal resists high winds, heavy snow loads, and wildfires without burning or rotting."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Utah Weather Performance"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Snow and Ice: Metal roofs shed snow quickly, which prevents heavy weight buildup. However, sliding snow can crash off the roof and damage landscaping or cars unless you install snow guards or fences. Asphalt shingles hold snow in place better, but ice dams can form during freeze-thaw cycles if attic heat melts the snow unevenly ."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Sun and Heat: Metal reflects solar radiant heat, keeping your attic cooler in the summer. Asphalt absorbs heat and degrades faster under harsh sun exposure."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Maintenance"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Asphalt Shingles: Requires periodic checks for missing, torn, or worn-out shingles, especially after severe storms."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Metal Roof: Demands very little upkeep\u2014mostly routine checks on fasteners and panel seals."
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
